    "body": "The `/v1/completions` streaming handler tracks cached tokens but omits them from `continuous_usage_stats` chunks. This adds `prompt_tokens_details` with the per-choice cached count when `--enable-cache-report` is enabled, including zero. Disabled reporting stays unchanged.\n\nAdds a handler regression test for zero, positive, and disabled-reporting cases. The response/final-stream and Chat zero-value fix is split into #44010; these PRs can merge independently.\n\nThanks to @rlrs for the earlier investigation and implementation in #20203.\n\nValidation: pre-commit and `git diff --check` passed. Isolated streaming checks passed for cache counts, reporting flags, repeated chunks, and multiple choices; the same checks reproduce the bug on `main`. Full registered handler tests were not run locally because PyTorch/FastAPI are unavailable.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38368450828](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38368450828)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38368450626](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38368450626)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38368450892](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38368450892)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
